{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Which pose and view the people engine draws a person in, by what they are doing and the kind of spot they are in. Read by src/presentation/appearance-engine/pose-chooser.ts; no code lists a pose. Each list is weighted (weight defaults to 1), and a person always gets the same pose for the same situation: the draw is a stable hash of their appearance seed, never a die and never the clock. A pose with no painting for the person's build or outfit is drawn as the pose it stands in for (standIn), then standing, so adding art never needs a code change.",
  "heldBack": {
    "fist-raised": "Both raised fists are cropped at the top of the painted canvas (hands cut off) on every build; repaint it with the arms lower before it is chosen.",
    "head-in-hand": "The painted hand covers the forehead and eyes, and the face layer is drawn over the body, so the hand would vanish behind the face; it needs a hand-over-face layer drawn above the head before it is chosen.",
    "laughing": "Not painted yet: its folder holds no bodies on any build; paint it where the standing head is before it is chosen.",
    "back-addressing": "Painted from behind, but the head sits 12 to 28 pixels from where the standing back body has it, so a hair layer would show a second head; repaint it with the head where the standing one is before it is chosen."
  },
